{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>I am YHWH your Elohim who brought you out, etc.</b> I am YHWH — and inasmuch as I am your Elohim, you recognize that I am that First Being who is fitting that you should serve Him and pray to Him." "<b>I brought you out of the land of Egypt.</b> In order that you may merit that I become your Elohim — that the continuity of your existence be from Him without intermediary; such existence does not change or perish in any way, as is the case with the existence of the other eternal beings." "<b>I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> I Myself, for this very end, have commanded you this commandment, in order that you may attain this intended goal, as it says: וִהְיִיתֶם קְדֹשִׁים לֵאלֹהֵיכֶם (Numbers 15:40)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:01.219746394Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}